<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    AppGarden's risk keyword database.

    Every entry under Categories is one threat category. Its Keywords are
    matched against the title, the description and the other metadata of a
    catalog item (name, categories, repository, link URLs); a word matches
    only as a whole word, so "ai" finds "AI workspace" and "Aarynwood" but
    never "available". Every match makes the Get button show an alert that
    carries ShortRisk and DisclaimerShort.

    The sentences are deliberately short and hedged. A keyword is a guess from
    a word someone typed, not a finding, and the alert says so: the panel has
    to leave the reader more able to judge the software than it found them.

    Adding a category: give it an Identifier, a Title, its ShortRisk sentence and its
    Keywords, then add a case to Tests/Unit/t_AGRiskAdviser.m. A category with
    no keywords, or with an empty sentence, is dropped when the file is read
    rather than shown as a blank warning.
-->
